From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:59:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: Start the display processors on system_dfl_wq

apple_drm_init_dcp() queues each processor's start on system_unbound_wq.
That queue is deprecated in this kernel, so every boot logs

  workqueue: work func apple_dcp_start_fn [appledrm] enqueued on
  deprecated workqueue. Use system_{percpu|dfl}_wq instead.

system_dfl_wq is the unbound queue under its new name, and the rest of
drm/apple already queues its work there. Use it for the starts too.
The starts still run concurrently and unbound, as before.

The readiness selftest mocked system_unbound_wq by name. Its queue_work()
mock now ignores the queue, so it runs each start whichever queue the
driver names.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

(cherry picked from commit b5e85dbab7372e34bdb5b51405aad2a5bc1e8e65)
[j604 backport: non-built files kept as in our tree: tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
index 9dce123c39..ba1f4d8be2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
@@ -1107,7 +1107,7 @@ static int apple_drm_init_dcp(struct device *dev)
 		connector_type[i] = dcp_get_connector_type(dcp[i]);
 		start[i].dcp = dcp[i];
 		INIT_WORK_ONSTACK(&start[i].work, apple_dcp_start_fn);
-		queue_work(system_unbound_wq, &start[i].work);
+		queue_work(system_dfl_wq, &start[i].work);
 	}
 	for (i = 0; i < num_dcp; i++) {
 		flush_work(&start[i].work);
